Z||000000||Formula 18||09-15-2000||12:02 AM||||Anyone know if this will work??? Pacesetter sell a set of mild steel headers that are supposed to go on a 3.4L camaro and I was wondering if these would fit in the engine bay. It would be nice. You can get Coated ones for about 300 but either way you'ld have to buy the cross over which I am pretty sure wouldn't work. <P>You'd probally have to fab up a new "y pipe" but I have to swap out that Oclet system for some stainless anyway.<P>------------------<BR>Brian<BR> -88 Formula||||reg||5
Z||000001||Standard||09-15-2000||02:56 AM||||I know Cooter used the stock camaro (i believe) headers when he did his 3.4 conversion, but he also had a full custom exhaust fabbed up.  With a bit of work anythings possible..<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">     <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker<p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 09-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||09-15-2000||11:05 PM||||yep- it can be done. But you had better have a good friend at the muffler shop! I have thought about getting the headers to replace my Camaro cast iron manifolds with, but for now I will wait. The camaro manifolds have larger ports and passages than the Fiero manifolds anyway, so I already have a good setup without the headers. And I dont think I will have the broken front manifold problem with the heat shields on the cast manifolds. When the engine comes out to replace the cheap clutch I stuck in there, I MAY see about adding the headers. If I do, I will post pics and info here.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula 18||09-16-2000||05:49 PM||||Cooter? <BR>Have you seen these 3.4 headers? Do you know if they'll even fit? If they fit and the primaies aren't huge this might be a good way to get rid of thoes leaky manifolds, espically if you wanna do a turbo ala Dennis and need a new Y-Pipe anyways. If anyonne has seen these LMK what you thought. <P><P>------------------<BR>Brian<BR> -88 Formula||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||09-16-2000||08:53 PM||||I have not seen the 3.4 headers, but since they are a bolt on for the Camaro, they would have to be the same diminsions as the cast manifolds. If that is true, they must be very short tube headers, and probably not much, if any, better than the manifolds. When I had the 3.4 out, I measured the port size on the Fiero and Camaro manifolds and the Camaro ones were bigger- I cant remember exactly how much, but bigger. When the batteries get charged back up in my camera, I will post some engine compartment pic's.||||reg||1
